TITLE:: RLCategory
summary:: Everything named arrows generate by composition, each with a shortest word: a monoid, a group, a category
categories:: Libraries>reLation
related:: Classes/RLRelation, Classes/RLTransform, Classes/RLRelationContext, Guides/reLation

DESCRIPTION::
The generators are link::Classes/RLRelation::s or link::Classes/RLTransform::s (anything that composes with code::<>::, compares by value and answers code::sourceIdentity::, code::targetIdentity:: and code::follows::). The category holds every arrow their compositions give, found breadth first, so each arrow comes with a shortest word: the list of generator names in the strong::order of time::.

Arrows on one list of objects generate a strong::monoid::; when every arrow can be undone, a strong::group::. Arrows between several lists generate a category with as many objects.

What it is for: the monoid knows the walks. Its arrows are all the different things a word can do, and code::relating(x, y):: lists those that take x to y. On the 24 triads and 4 augmented triads of 12 steps:

table::
## generators || arrows
## S, one voice by a semitone || 7 (S7 = S5)
## T, two voices by a semitone each || 4
## S and T || 8
## D, two common tones || 6
## U, P, L (Cube Dance with its edges named) || 40
::

code::
~cd = RLRelationContext.cubeDance;
~m = ~cd.category;                                   // RLCategory([[\U, u], [\P, p], [\L, l]])
~m.size;                                             // 40
~m.wordOf(~m.generator(\L) <> ~m.generator(\P));     // [P, L]
~m.arrow([\U, \U, \U]) == ~m.generator(\U);          // true
~m.invertibles.collect { |a| ~m.wordOf(a) };         // [], [P], [L], [P, L], [L, P], [P, L, P]
~m.relating(~cd.space.major(2), ~cd.space.minor(7)); // six arrows relate D major to G minor: UU, UPU ...

~ctx = RLChordContext(RLChordSpace.triads(RLEDO(12)));
~plr = RLCategory([[\P, ~ctx.p], [\L, ~ctx.l], [\R, ~ctx.r]]);
[~plr.size, ~plr.isGroup];                           // [24, true]
~plr.wordOf(~ctx.t(6));                              // four steps: the tritone is a product of P, L, R
~plr.includes(~ctx.t(7));                            // false: a fifth is not
::

The closure is guarded: more than strong::maxSize:: arrows is an Error. A monoid of relations can be very large (nearly a million with sus4 chords on one list).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: generators
An Array of code::[name, arrow]:: pairs (or Associations).
argument:: maxSize
4000 by default.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: names
The generators' names, in the order given.

METHOD:: generator
A generator by its name.

METHOD:: arrows
Every arrow: the identities first, then by the length of their words. Each has its word as label, written right to left ("LP" is P first), "id" for an identity.

METHOD:: identities
The identity arrows, one per list of objects.

METHOD:: size
The number of arrows.

METHOD:: wordOf
The shortest word of an arrow, in time order; nil when it is not one of the arrows.

METHOD:: words
Every arrow's word, in the order of link::#-arrows::.

METHOD:: arrow
The arrow of a word (time order). An Error when its steps do not follow one another.

METHOD:: includes
METHOD:: indexOf
Whether something is one of the arrows; its place among them.

METHOD:: composeIndex
The index of code::arrows[i]:: after code::arrows[j]::, nil when they do not follow one another. Read from the generators' table: no relation is composed.

METHOD:: table
The whole table of compositions, by indices.

METHOD:: isMonoid
One list of objects, one identity.

METHOD:: invertibles
The arrows that can be undone.

METHOD:: isGroup
A monoid whose arrows can all be undone.

METHOD:: relating
The arrows that take x to y (for relations: that relate them).
